'''Gale Torg''' also known as '''Galen Torg''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[sergeant]] assigned to guard and escort [[senator]]s and dignitaries who visited the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]'s headquarters in the [[Great Temple]] on [[Yavin 4]]. He carried a [[DH-17 blaster pistol]] and wore the uniform of [[Alderaanian consular security]], which featured a service [[Armor|helmet]] with flash visor and integral [[comlink]] and a multi-pocketed spacer vest of [[Corellian]] cut.<ref name="UVG" />

During the [[Battle of Yavin]], the Alliance managed to destroy the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[planet]]-[[Death|killing]] [[superweapon]], the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], in the [[Yavin system]]. During the [[Royal Award Ceremony|ceremony]] held to honor the Heroes of Yavin at the Great Temple, Torg served as a [[Rebel Honor Guard]], standing in front of the [[Grand Temple's throne room|audience room's]] entrance.<ref name="ANH">{{Film|IV}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:GalenTorg-ANH.png|thumb|left|200px|Gale Torg as he appears in Rebel Honor Guard uniform in ''A New Hope''.]]
Gale Torg first appeared, retroactively, in the [[1977]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="ANH" /> The character then went onto appear&mdash;again unnamed&mdash;in the film's [[2016]] prequel, ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="RO1">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

Gale Torg's introduction into [[canon]] was brought about by his origins in [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] as [[Galen Torg]],<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/816058561998372865|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|quote=p. 59. Gale Torg was inspired by the old WEG character from Galaxy Guide 1 Galen Torg, but there's already one Galen in this story.|archivefile=File:TwitterCap_pablohidalgo_RogueOneUVGdump.png}}</ref> who was identified as one of the [[Rebel Honor Guard/Legends|Rebel Honor Guards]] seen in ''A New Hope''.<ref name="CCG">{{CCG|set=Premiere Limited|cardname=Rebel Guard}}</ref> The name was first used in [[1995]]'s ''[[Galaxy Guide 1: A New Hope]]'', where the name was simply used to represent a typical [[Rebel trooper/Legends|rebel soldier]],<ref name="GG1">''[[Galaxy Guide 1: A New Hope]]''</ref> before being connected to the film character by the [[Star Wars Customizable Card Game|''Star Wars'' Customizable Card Game]].<ref name="CCG" /> In using the name for a character seen in ''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story'', ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]'' author [[Pablo Hidalgo]] realized that the film already included a prominent character,<ref name="Twitter" /> the [[scientist]]<ref name="RO1" /> [[Galen Walton Erso]], with the first name Galen, so he decided to change Torg's first name.<ref name="Twitter" />

